In contrast, the term endangered language refers to a language with a certain degree of danger for its existence. Endangered languages are relevant for our study, as most Indigenous languages are also endangered (Hale, 1992). According to the UNESCO classification, (Moseley, 2010) languages can be sorted into the following different categories:

- safe: spoken by all generations;

